    "title": "Samsung Messages being discontinued: Galaxy users transition to Google",
    "text": "A man walks past the Samsung logo in this 2025 file photo.JUNG YEON-JE/AFP via Getty ImagesSamsung Messages app will be discontinued as company shifts users to Google Messages, the phone announced on its Website.Samsung has not announced an exact date for when the app will be discontinued, but announced it will shut down its Messages app in July 2026 and make Google Messages the default messaging app.AdvertisementArticle continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢How do I switch from Samsung Messages to Google Messages?Many Samsung users will receive an in-app notification to guide them through the switch. Others who do not receive the notification will need to manually follow the steps to switch to Google Messages.Steps: Open or download Google Messages.2. Make Google Messages your default SMS app. When you open the app for the first time, it will ask whether you want to make it the default.3. Select Google Messages.4. Tap “Set as default.” Will all Samsung devices be affected?Galaxy S26 and newer devices cannot download Samsung Messages from the Galaxy Store, according to the company. Other devices will no longer be able to download the app after it is discontinued in July 2026.AdvertisementArticle continues below this adWant more Houston Chronicle?Make us a Preferred Source on Google to see more of us when you search.Add Preferred SourceDevices running Android 11 or older will not be affected by the change and will still be able to use Samsung Messages.Sign up for The 713Start your day and stay informed with essential Houston news.By signing up, you agree to our Terms Of Use and acknowledge that your information will be used as described in our Privacy Policy.",
